From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaoyi Liu <liuchaoyi@akane.waseda.jp>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:17:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] usage: an Antigravity desktop step's speed, from its first
 token and end
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Antigravity desktop app's rows on the Usage page and in `magpie usage`
had tokens but no TTFT and no tok/s, while Codex's beside them had both.
The app's conversation database has the times for it: a step's metadata
holds field 1 (its start), 6 (its first token) and 8 (its end), each a
Timestamp. Only field 1 was read.

Before: an antigravity call had Millis and TTFT 0, so no speed and no floor.
After: readAntigravityCalls keeps Millis = end - start and TTFT = first -
start (agAppCall.times). A step with no end, or an end before its start,
tells no time; a first token outside start..end is dropped and the step
keeps its time alone.

Gemini can send a step's tool call whole: a real step on this machine wrote
599 tokens 0.3 s after a first token at 16.6 s, and yygutn's step 1 on
#2190 (the existing fixture) 621 tokens in 9 ms. So a step is held to a
Codex turn's bounds, CodexWindowMs and CodexBodyTokens
(usage.Row.antigravityStep, page.js ledAntigravityStep), and antigravity
joins FloorAgents / LED_FLOOR_AGENTS: its time runs from the step's start,
before the model is asked, so output over it is a floor.
The antigravity call parse version goes to 2 so cached calls are read again.

Run at this head (rebased on origin/main ec7a18d12):
- go test ./internal/sessions ./internal/usage: ok.
- go test ./internal/gui (before the rebase, on 7cce4b4d7): TestLaneLimitRoutes and
  TestPanelHiddenByWailsMarksPageOutOfSight fail, and fail the same on
  origin/main 7cce4b4d7 (just fetched) on this machine (macOS 27; the lane
  test reads the lanes of the magpie running here). Not run again after
  the rebase.
- node --test usage-antigravity-speed (new): 22 of 22, Chromium and WebKit,
  five languages; usage-speed-count and usage-ledger-ttft: 64 of 64.
- gofmt -l and GOOS=linux/windows go vet on the two packages: clean.
- Broken by hand: the Decode/FloorAgents change reverted, the new usage
  test is red on 4 rows; Millis/TTFT zeroed, TestAntigravityAppCallTimes
  is red.
- Real data: this branch's `magpie usage today` in a sandbox HOME with
  copies of today's 33 conversation databases (Antigravity 2.x, macOS):
  Antigravity ttft 13.7 s · 117 tok/s, gemini-4-argon 115, gemini-3.8-flash
  392. An independent Python read of the same databases with the same
  bounds: 670 of 2,157 steps measured, 117.4 tok/s.

Not tried: the Insiders store (same reader), Windows or Linux Antigravity.
Not known: whether field 6 is the first thought or the first answer token;
output counts thoughts as the gateway counts a Gemini reply, and Reasoning
stays unset as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Co-authored-by: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com> (rebased onto aa3d11d5b; independently verified)
